cal_business_count":2},{"category":"Nightlife","historical_business_count":5},{"category":"Modern European","historical_business_count":0},{"category":"Steakhouses","historical_business_count":0}],"history":[{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"American (New), Bars, Cocktail Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":5},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Bars, Cocktail Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"American (New), Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"LG03thDHBO4vRcYZ7g_zmg","review_id":"fYC2hmuc4tWjkMYqRaDIPw","date":"2019-04-19T20:03:53","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9389388561248779,"text_excerpt":"This place was fabulous hands down! We stayed in the French Quarter and the place is about 15 mins walking, which was nice. It's located in the Warehouse District. briquette is known seafood and the place is expansive! They have a sommelier on site (Stephen), who answered all my wine questions and we tried a new wine that was lush and simply amazing. The best part is that it was $26 for the bottle! Appetizers: gumbo, which was very tasty but not spicy. A little Tabasco did the trick. For $10, they could give you more...it's a tad pricey. (4/5) The oysters with shrimp on top were plated beautifully and very good (5/5). At $16 it is pricey for 4 oysters. DINNER: I ordered redfish ($32) with..."},{"business_id":"LG03thDHBO4vRcYZ7g_zmg","review_id":"tL6IJliy-5v66y2n5oZufg","date":"2019-05-30T23:10:48","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9317993521690369,"text_excerpt":"Really good spot in the art district in New Orleans. Service was impeccable and the ambiance was really nice. I had the Oysters Rockefeller to start and they were excellent. 4 were on the plate and I've never had them like this. They cover them with a spinach sauce almost. Really tasty! For the entree I had the Roasted Duckling Girod. I believe this place is known for their fish but I figured the oysters were good enough and I took a flyer on this dish. Wow, I'm glad I did. Cooked to perfection and topped with their homemade raspberry purée, which really made it into a first rate dish. For desert I had the Dark Chocolate Crème Brûlée which was excellent. Great place and highly recommend i..."},{"business_id":"LG03thDHBO4vRcYZ7g_zmg","review_id":"8nJa4lkysThvcT4vCd7kDA","date":"2020-02-13T21:02:20","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9302204847335815,"text_excerpt":"We tried this place through Groupon. The food and service were fantastic. We wouldn't have come to known this place otherwise. The ambience is superb and the building has nice gas lights. We tried market catch sandwich and Briquette pasta. The waiter suggested items and drinks after listening to our preferences. The taste buds were truly satisfied. Try to get out of FrencH quarter and taste some great food in warehouse district."}],